msgid "Effect"
msgstr ""

msgid "Any <a> tag, or any wrapper element (div, section…) that contains an <a>"
msgstr ""

msgid "Records a click entry (URL + timestamp) whenever a visitor clicks the element. The URL is taken from the <a href> — either the element itself or the first anchor found inside it. Navigation is not interrupted."
msgstr ""

msgid "How to add the class in WordPress"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the block editor: select the link text, open the link toolbar, click the three-dot menu → \"Edit link\" → expand \"Advanced\" → add the class in the \"CSS class\" field."
msgstr ""

msgid "In the classic editor or a page builder code/HTML module: switch to HTML view and add the class directly on the <a> element."
msgstr ""

msgid "In Divi — plain text link: select the link → link settings → CSS class field."
msgstr ""

msgid "In Divi — Image or other module with a link: open the module settings → Advanced tab → CSS ID & Classes → CSS Class field. The class goes on the module wrapper div, which contains the <a> Divi generates automatically."
msgstr ""

