msgstr ""

msgid "[pcio_me_event]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders an event card with cover image, title, date, location, description, and sign-up buttons for logged-in members."
msgstr ""

msgid "The numeric ID of the event (required). Find it in the URL when viewing an event at /vis/events/{id}/."
msgstr ""

msgid "What is rendered"
msgstr ""

msgid "Cover image (if one has been uploaded via the Photos tab on the event detail page)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Event title, date / time range, and location"
msgstr ""

msgid "Event description (rich text)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sign-up buttons (Joining / Interested / Not joining) — shown only to logged-in users with the"
msgstr ""

msgid "capability who are also linked to a member record."
msgstr ""

msgid "[pcio_me_events]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Shows all upcoming events as a responsive grid of tiles. The number of tiles per row adapts automatically to the screen width. Each tile shows the square thumbnail (falling back to the banner image), a date badge, the title, date / time and location, and links to the public event page at /events/{slug}/. No login required."
msgstr ""

msgid "Maximum number of upcoming events to display."
msgstr ""

msgid "yes / no"
msgstr ""

msgid "Whether to show the live search box above the tiles for filtering by title and location."
msgstr ""

msgid "A responsive grid of tiles — the number of columns adjusts to the available width."
msgstr ""

msgid "Only upcoming events are listed, ordered by start date. Past days are excluded."
msgstr ""

msgid "Each tile uses the square Thumb image, falling back to the Banner image, then a coloured placeholder using the event colour."
msgstr ""

msgid "An optional search box filters the tiles instantly as the visitor types."
msgstr ""

msgid "[pcio_me_event_roller]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Rotating front-page slider that automatically shows the next upcoming events from the calendar. Each slide shows the cover image, an overlaid title and date, and a Read More button linking to the public event page. No login required."
msgstr ""

msgid "How many upcoming events to include in the slider."
msgstr ""

msgid "Seconds between automatic slide changes. The timer resets when a visitor uses the arrows."
msgstr ""

msgid "How events are chosen"
msgstr ""

msgid "Events are selected automatically — the next events ordered by start date."
msgstr ""

msgid "Only the date part of the start time is compared, so events happening today are still shown. Past days are excluded."
msgstr ""

msgid "Events without a cover image show a coloured placeholder using the event colour."
msgstr ""

msgid "Visitors can move between slides with the left / right arrows; otherwise it advances on its own."
msgstr ""

msgid "[pcio_me_upcoming_events]"
msgstr ""

msgid "A compact “agenda” list of upcoming events grouped by month. Each month is shown as a heading, followed by its events as “day. title”, with the title linking to the public event page. Month names follow the site language (e.g. September / Oktober / November in Danish). No login required."
msgstr ""

msgid "How many months ahead to include, counting the current month (3 = this month plus the next two)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Optional hard cap on the number of events shown. 0 means no cap — every event in the window is listed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Events from the start of today up to the end of the month window are listed, ordered by start date."
msgstr ""

msgid "Events are grouped under their start month; the year is added to the heading only when the window crosses into another year."
msgstr ""

msgid "Only the date part of the start time is compared, so events happening today are still shown."
msgstr ""

msgid "[pcio_me_newsletters]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Shows a list of the most recently generated newsletter PDFs, each linking to the public PDF document. Newsletters are produced from the Mails screen by ticking “This mail is a newsletter” and clicking “Generate newsletter PDF”."
msgstr ""

msgid "How many recent newsletters to list."
msgstr ""

msgid "[pcio_me_member_count]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Displays the current total number of members as an animated count-up number. Each page render is recorded as a front-page view in the Statistics dashboard. Works in any page builder text or code module (e.g. Divi Text Module)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Note"
msgstr ""

msgid "To track sponsor link clicks from this page, add the CSS class "
msgstr ""

msgid " to any anchor tag in your content. Clicks are recorded automatically and shown under Vis → Statistics. See Vis → Sponsor Links for details."
msgstr ""

msgid "[pcio_me_member_signup]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders a public registration form for new members. With no payment extension active the member is created immediately and a welcome email is sent. Active extensions can inject extra fields and add a payment (checkout) step on submission."
msgstr ""

msgid "The welcome email is sent from the system mail template labelled \"member_welcome\" under Vis → Mails. Edit the subject and body there, using the tag chips to insert dynamic values."
msgstr ""

msgid "string (URL)"
msgstr ""

msgid "URL the visitor is sent to if they abandon the Stripe payment step. Relative paths are converted to absolute HTTPS automatically. Ignored when no payment extension is active."
msgstr ""

